# 6. DESIGN A DOCUMENTED LOSSLESS ARCHIVE FORMAT

Create a custom, versioned, human-readable text format.

Suggested format:

TREEVAULT_V1
TOKENS: 9

V:A
V:B
N
V:D
N
N
V:C
N
N

FORMAT RULES:

- TREEVAULT_V1 identifies the archive format version.
- TOKENS specifies the number of serialized tokens.
- V: indicates a node value.
- N indicates a missing child.
- Every token occupies a separate line.
- Everything after the V: prefix is the node label.
- Labels must be non-empty and must not contain newline characters.

The format must preserve labels and tree shape.

Define and document:

- Header validation.
- Token count validation.
- Node token validation.
- Null marker handling.
- Empty label handling.
- Incomplete input handling.
- Extra token handling.
- Unsupported version handling.

An archive must be rejected if it is malformed or incomplete.

Do not silently restore a partial tree.

Do not confuse a legitimate node label with the null marker.

Implement transactional restoration: if validation or reconstruction fails, do not expose a partially reconstructed tree as a successful result.

The archive must be sufficient to reconstruct the tree without access to the original in-memory object.

An empty tree must also have a well-defined representation.

